				77,
				1
			],
			"Message": "chore(Grove): Sync Documentation/Rust submodule\n\nUpdate the `Documentation/Rust` submodule from commit 6c75823 to c65b8f6. This sync pulls in the latest upstream Rust documentation standards and reference materials to ensure the Grove extension host documentation remains aligned with current best practices.\n\nVerify that external documentation references and resource links in the local Grove documentation tree stay consistent with the upstream Rust project guidelines.",
			"SHA": "cf787f11a950ece08addf31b48f45faf7128c6a9"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
			"Date": "2026-05-19T04:15:43Z",
			"File": [
				"⠁⠀⠀⠀⠀",
				77,
				1
			],
			"Message": "docs(Grove): Expand architecture diagram with module-level detail\n\nThe Mermaid diagram in README.md had grown stale, showing only a coarse-grained view of Grove's internal architecture. The new diagram reflects the actual Rust module layout with three properly grouped subsystems:\n\n- Host/: Extension lifecycle (ExtensionHost, ExtensionManager, Activation, Lifecycle, APIBridge)\n- WASM/: WASMtime runtime stack (Runtime, ModuleLoader, MemoryManager, HostBridge)\n- Transport/: Strategy pattern (gRPCTransport, IPCTransport, WASMTransport) with the Strategy trait\n- Protocol/: SpineConnection as the Spine protocol client\n\nAlso adds the complementary Cocoon subgraph showing the shared API surface between the native WASM extension host and the Node.js sidecar, and documents both gRPC (:50052) and Unix socket IPC transport paths to Mountain.\n\nColor classes are updated with explicit fill/stroke/text colors for accessibility across light terminals. This provides contributors with an accurate, navigable map of the codebase structure.",
			"SHA": "9c28e65e5b47e096543c8bbabceff48d5c9231d4"
		},
		{
			"Author": "Nikola Hristov",
